  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather with above normal temperatures through\nthe weekend under high pressure.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nSfc ridge of high pressure will keep winds light, skies mostly \nclear and temperatures above normal through the weekend. Highs \nwill be in the mid-80s on Saturday and lower 80s on Sunday for \ninland locations, cooler along the coast with a sea breeze \ndeveloping each afternoon. \n\nCannot rule out patchy river valley fog the next 2 nights as\nradn/l cooling occurs. Have lowered temps below guidance for \ntonight as temps this morning undercut NBM numbers by about 2-5 \ndegrees.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Potential for a system moving in early next \nweek, bringing another round of wetting rainfall.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure lingers over the region this weekend, as low \npressure system slides along the east coast early next week. \nGenerally, low pressure east of the Carolinas moves northeast in\nthe Atlantic, east of Nova Scotia. To the north, another low \npressure over Canada moves eastward, bringing a cold front along\nits boundary. Wetting rainfall expected, with higher totals \nalong Downeast, Tuesday into Wednesday. There could be a chance \nof thunderstorms along the frontal boundary Tuesday night into \nWednesday.",
